# EVERY TABLE THE `pm` SCHEMA ACTUALLY HAS, READ FROM THE CATALOGUE. One row per table.
#
# ⭐⭐⭐ THE POPULATION OF THE DOMAIN-OBJECT CONTRACT, AND THE DATABASE IS THE ONLY HONEST SOURCE
#    FOR IT. diagrams/domain_objects.sqlc declares what each relational object renders as; this is
#    what there is to declare about. Parsing `CREATE TABLE` out of the `.ddl` would be a second
#    reading of the same file the schema was loaded from, so a table added and never loaded would
#    still appear and the contract would agree with a database that does not exist.
#
# ⛔ IT IS THE ONE RELATION HERE THAT READS OUTSIDE `pm`, and it is the reason: a contract needs a
#   population it did not write. `information_schema` is SQL-standard and every engine has it.
-- information_schema.tables restricted to the schema this model owns.
SELECT t.table_name::text AS object
FROM information_schema.tables t
WHERE t.table_schema = 'pm' AND t.table_type = 'BASE TABLE'
